      "side": 1,
      "message": "[From Jetski review] Checking only direct \u0027private_deps_\u0027 misses local exceptions where the included header belongs to a transitive \u0027public_deps\u0027 of a private dep (very common with wrapper targets like mojom/proto groups):\n\n  App --[deps]--\u003e T (check_includes_strict \u003d true) --[private_deps]--\u003e Wrapper --[public_deps]--\u003e GenTarget (hard_dep)\n\nIf T\u0027s public header includes GenTarget\u0027s generated header and \u0027.gn\u0027 has \u0027{ includer \u003d \"//path:T\", included \u003d \"//path:GenTarget\" }\u0027:\n1. HeaderChecker passes because \u0027HasException(T, GenTarget)\u0027 is true and \u0027kPermittedIgnoringStrict\u0027 walks \u0027private_deps\u0027 on T followed by \u0027public_deps\u0027 on Wrapper.\n2. However, \u0027HasLocalException(T, Wrapper)\u0027 here returns false, leaving \u0027check_includes_strict_optimizations_ \u003d true\u0027 on T and dropping GenTarget\u0027s hard_dep from App.\n\nTo handle transitive \u0027public_deps\u0027 without an O(V * E) walk across all targets, consider e.g. collecting the matched \u0027to\u0027 labels for \u0027label()\u0027 up front (skipping the walk entirely when empty, which is almost all targets) or memoizing reachable local-exception targets in ResolvedTargetData.\n\n(Minor typo on line 645: \u0027purely on optimization\u0027 -\u003e \u0027purely an optimization\u0027.)",
